## 3. Independent-review requirement

The complete R5 bundle must receive a fresh full atomic independent review.
The reviewer must read and hash every declared input, execute every fixed
offline command and independently attack:

- substitution of the frozen protected-source contract, decision or receipt;
- a changed sealed tree;
- tuple omission, insertion, replacement, reordering or duplication;
- restoration of `G03_NAME_ONLY_SCAN`, generic enumeration or scanner code;
- false claims that protected facts were observed or recomputed in R5;
- any Host, runtime, worktree, payload or effect authority.

## 4. Future decision boundary

`PASS_NO_BLOCKER` would not execute or freeze R5. Jenn would still need a
separate atomic freeze decision.

Even a later R5 freeze would not authorize `--actual`; a future source run
would require another exact, current Jenn execution decision bound to the
accepted R5 bytes and receipt v0.2.

